# TradePro — Production Startup Guide

## Prerequisites
- Node.js, npm, Python installed
- Docker Desktop running (for PostgreSQL & Redis)
- MT5 Terminal open (for live trading features)

---

## Step 1: Start Infrastructure (Docker)

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\sruja.SUNNULINGEGOWDA\Desktop\Backtesting"
docker-compose up -d postgres redis
```

This starts **PostgreSQL** (port `5433`) and **Redis** (port `6379`).

---

## Step 2: Build & Start Backend — NestJS API (port 3000)

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\sruja.SUNNULINGEGOWDA\Desktop\Backtesting\backend"
npm run build
node dist/src/main
```

> [!NOTE]
> The `start:prod` script in package.json uses `node dist/main`, but the actual compiled output is at `dist/src/main.js`. Use `node dist/src/main` directly.

---

## Step 3: Build & Start Frontend — Next.js (port 3002)

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\sruja.SUNNULINGEGOWDA\Desktop\Backtesting\trading-platform-frontend"
npm run build
npx next start --port 3002
```

---

## Step 4: Start MT5 Node.js Bridge (port 3001)

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\sruja.SUNNULINGEGOWDA\Desktop\Backtesting\mt5-server"
npm start
```

---

## Step 5: Start Python MT5 Bridge (port 8765)

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\sruja.SUNNULINGEGOWDA\Desktop\Backtesting\mt5-server\python-bridge"
python websocket_server.py
```

---

## Access

| Service | URL |
|---------|-----|
| **Website** | http://localhost:3002 |
| **API** | http://localhost:3000 |
| **MT5 REST** | http://localhost:3001/api/mt5 |
| **MT5 WebSocket** | ws://localhost:3001/ws/mt5 |
| **Python Bridge** | ws://localhost:8765 |

## Optional: Monitoring (Prometheus + Grafana)

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\sruja.SUNNULINGEGOWDA\Desktop\Backtesting"
docker-compose up -d prometheus grafana
```
- Grafana: http://localhost:3003 (admin / admin)
